## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design high-throughput concurrent queues under contention, covering memory reclamation, false sharing, and backpressure—critical for scalable data platforms at large-scale storage and analytics workloads.

## Key Concepts
- Lock-free queue basics, per-thread locality, and work-stealing semantics
- ABA avoidance via versioned pointers or sequence counters
- Hazard pointers or epoch-based reclamation for memory safety
- Cache-line alignment and padding to reduce false sharing
- Bounded capacity and spill-over strategies for backpressure

## Code Example
```c
typedef struct node {
  void* data;
  _Atomic(struct node*) next;
  int stamp; // version counter
} node_t;

typedef struct wsq {
  _Atomic(node_t*) head;
  _Atomic(node_t*) tail;
  // per-thread deques omitted for brevity
} wsq_t;
```

